<h2>What Forebet predictions cover</h2>
<p>Forebet's today page leads with 1X2 probabilities and adds short statistical trends, such as a run of away defeats or a sequence of matches going over a goal line. Alongside that it surfaces featured matches and goal-market context rather than a single recommended bet per fixture.</p>
<p>A probability split is not the same as a tip. A 48% away reading still leaves the majority of outcomes elsewhere, which is why the same fixture can justify a Double Chance card instead of a straight 2. On this Bao board each fixture gets one recommended market — 1X2, Double Chance, BTTS, Over/Under or HT/FT — with the reason written out, so you can see why the goals market was preferred over the result, or the reverse.</p>

<h2>How to assess a Forebet tip</h2>
<p>Read the forecast, then check the fixture underneath it:</p>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Recent form:</strong> the last six matches, weighted by opponent quality rather than raw wins.</li>
  <li><strong>Home/away record:</strong> venue splits often explain why a probability looks generous.</li>
  <li><strong>League position:</strong> useful when a real points gap exists, less so in a congested table.</li>
  <li><strong>Head-to-head:</strong> supporting evidence only; old meetings can involve different squads.</li>
  <li><strong>Team news:</strong> confirmed injuries and suspensions, not rumoured ones.</li>
  <li><strong>Market fit:</strong> whether the evidence points at a result market or a goals market.</li>
</ul>
